1) Declaration+Allocation

Unordered Set(hash-based, no sorting)
1)unordered_set<int>mySet1;
2)unordered_set<int>mySet2={1,2,3};

Ordered Set(BST-based,sorted)
1)set<int>mySet1;
2)set<int>mySet2={1,2,3};

2)Adding an element
1)s.insert(element);

3)Adding all elements
1)mySet1.insert(mySet2.begin(),mySet2.end());

4)Remove an element 
1)mySet.erase(element);

5)Getting the size 
1)mySet.size();

6)Two sets are equal or not
1)mySet1==myset2;

7) Checking Existence
1)set1.find(element)!=set1.end(); ->bool 
2)set.count(element); ->1/0 size_t/int    size_t -> int gadbad kre toh size_t use krna hai int ki jagah  

8) Sum of set
1)int sum=accumulate(s.begin(),s.end(),0);

9) Max of set 
1)int max=*max_element(mySet.begin(),mySet.end());

10)Min of set
1)int min=*min_element(mySet.begin(),mySet.end());

11) Looping set
1) for(int val:mySet) {cout<<val;}  ->int ki jagah auto use kr skte hai har datatype le leta hai 

12)Union of sets 
1)set1.insert(set2.begin(),set2.end());

13) Intersection of sets 
1)unordered_set<int>newSet;
  for(auto num:Set1){
    if(Set2.count(num))
    {newSet.insert(num);}} 

14) Difference of set 
1)unordered_set<int>diffSet;
  for(auto num:Set1){
    if(!Set2.count(num))
    {diffSet.insert(num);}}    
    